BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Calendar Ics": "https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopening"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_calendar_ics
X-SOURCE:Warren Wilson College
DTSTAMP:20260905T040524Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53886473896943
DTSTART:20261002T230000Z
DTEND:20261003T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:On Friday October 2nd\, Warren Wilson College celebrates the gr
 and reopening of Kittredge Arts Center\, with renowned Bluegrass act Siste
 r Sadie headlining!  The Kittredge Arts Center grand reopening is part of 
 the Warren Wilson College's 2026 Homecoming\, and is also a homecoming for
  Sister Sadie's mandolinist\, WWC alum' Rainy Miatke (Music Major\, Class 
 of 2025).\n\n \n\n \n\nTickets can be purchased here:  https://wwc-venture
 s.ticketspice.com/sister-sadie-and-the-kittredge-arts-center-grand-reopeni
 ng \n\n \n\nFor more information abuot the event\, please contact Dr. Jaso
 n DeCristofaro at jdecristofaro@warren-wilson.edu or (828)545-3916.  \n\n 
 \n\n \n\nSister Sadie Bio:\n\nWhat started as an accidental band became a 
 force. GRAMMY-nominated. IBMA-decorated. Opry-validated. But for all the\n
 accolades\, they were often reduced to one line: an all-female bluegrass b
 and. True—but never the point. Sister Sadie has always\nbeen about the m
 usic. The fire. The truth.\n\n\nTheir new album\, All Will Be Well\, is th
 at truth—loud\, fearless\, and free. You’ll hear echoes of bluegrass\,
  but what rises is\nsomething bigger: country with claws\, Americana with 
 muscle\, gospel grit and raw storytelling.\n\n\nFrom the haunting “Prodi
 gal Daughter” to the swagger of “Do What You Want” and the aching be
 auty of “If I Don’t Have You\,”\nthese six women are not performing 
 roles—they’re telling you who they are.\n\n\nThis is Sister Sadie\, ev
 olved: bold\, bonded\, and braver than ever. They're not asking for space.
  They're taking it.\n\n\nAnd they’re just getting started.\n\n \n\nAbout
  Kittredge Arts Center:\n\nNestled within the beautiful\, historic Warren 
 Wilson College campus\, the Kittredge Arts Center provides a centralized l
 ocation for the arts at WWC and WNC. The Center features the 321-seat Kitt
 redge Theater and 80-seat Williams Recital Hall\, where music and performa
 nce events are featured throughout the year. Kittredge Arts Center is also
  available as a rental space to organizations looking for an affordable op
 tion in a beautiful location for conferences\, business retreats\, and oth
 er events. \n\n \n\nFor more information\, please contact Dr. Jason DeCris
 tofaro (Assistant Professor of Music\, Music Department Chair\, and Direct
 or of Kittredge Arts Center) at 828-273-8254 or jdecristofaro@warren-wilso
 n.edu
GEO:35.613818;-82.438862
LOCATION:Kittredge Arts Center\, Kittredge Theater
SUMMARY:Sister Sadie & the Kittredge Arts Center Grand Reopening
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/sister-sadie-the-kittr
 edge-arts-center-grand-reopening
CATEGORIES:Performance
END:VEVENT
